# A page app's phase follows the page, as a Linux app's follows its window
# and the machine (NativeApp/the_phase_follows_hide_show_and_suspend_on_linux).
# Before launch the app has no phase; launch starts its run, which hears
# that the document shows. The page (page.mjs) hides the document and shows
# it again (visibilitychange), the browser freezes the page and resumes it
# (the Page Lifecycle API's freeze and resume), and the page goes away
# (pagehide). The app's lifecycle listener hears each change in order, one
# at a time, with the phase already published.
requires: tool:node
fixture: ThePhaseFollowsHideShowAndSuspendInAPage.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet build --target web main.jet
exit: 0
copy: page.mjs .jet/build/page.mjs
step: node page.mjs
cwd: .jet/build
exit: 0
stdout: = "before launch: no phase\n1 VisibilityChanged: Unknown Running -> Visible Running, run 1, phase 1\nlaunched\n2 VisibilityChanged: Visible Running -> Hidden Running, run 1, phase 2\n3 VisibilityChanged: Hidden Running -> Visible Running, run 1, phase 3\n4 SleepPreparing: Visible Running -> Visible Suspending, run 1, phase 4\n5 Woke: Visible Suspending -> Visible Running, run 1, phase 5\n6 Closing: Visible Running -> Hidden Running, run 1, phase 6\n"
